SUPERMARKET CHECKOUT DISCOUNT

Supermarket Checkout Discount — a real-world task using only today's concepts: combining conditions with and / or / not, comparisons (==, !=, <, >, <=, >=), if / elif / else, variables, input(), converting input (int, float), basic arithmetic, and printing with 2-decimal money format. No imports, no tricks.

Solve it individually, then come together as a group to compare approaches. Good luck!

A supermarket in Port Harcourt is running a checkout promo. Their billing program must work out the discount a customer has earned and the final amount they pay.

The program asks three things: the basket total (decimals allowed), whether the customer is a loyalty member (yes/no), and whether today is a promo day (yes/no). Answers are typed in lowercase, exactly yes or no.

The store's discount rules:

- Members always get 10% off.
- Non-members get 5% off, but only if their basket is 50000 or more.
- On promo days, any customer who already earned a discount gets an extra 5% on top. A customer with no discount gets nothing extra, promo day or not.
- Delivery fee: 2500 if the basket is under 20000, free if it is 20000 or more. The fee does not care about membership or discounts.

The program must print four lines: the discount percent, the discount amount in naira, the delivery fee, and the final amount to pay (basket minus discount plus delivery), all money values with two decimal places.

Sample run 1:

Basket total: 32000
Loyalty member (yes/no): yes
Promo day (yes/no): yes

DISCOUNT: 15%
DISCOUNT AMOUNT: N4800.00
DELIVERY FEE: N0.00
FINAL TOTAL: N27200.00

Sample run 2:

Basket total: 18500
Loyalty member (yes/no): no
Promo day (yes/no): no

DISCOUNT: 0%
DISCOUNT AMOUNT: N0.00
DELIVERY FEE: N2500.00
FINAL TOTAL: N21000.00

Edge cases to handle: a non-member at exactly 50000 on a promo day (10% total), a non-member at 49999 on a promo day (still 0%), a basket at exactly 20000 (free delivery), a member with a small basket on a normal day (10%, pay delivery), and a basket total of exactly 0.
